  ('Universal benefits', 'benefits paid to everyone in a category regardless of income.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Means-tested benefits', 'benefits paid only to those whose income/wealth falls below a specified level.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Universal basic income (UBI)', 'a regular, unconditional cash payment given to all citizens regardless of other income.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Derived demand (for labour)', 'demand for labour that arises from the demand for the goods/services labour produces.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Marginal revenue product (MRP)', 'the additional revenue generated by employing one more unit of a factor of production (MRP = MPP × MR).', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Wage and non-wage factors', 'wage factors are pay-related; non-wage factors include working conditions, job satisfaction and fringe benefits, which affect labour supply.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Trade union', 'an organisation of workers that negotiates collectively with employers over wages and conditions.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('National minimum wage', 'a legally binding minimum wage set by the government.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Monopsony', 'a market with a single (or dominant) buyer of a good or factor, such as labour.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Wage differentials', 'differences in wages paid to different workers/occupations, determined by labour market forces.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Transfer earnings', 'the minimum payment required to keep a factor of production in its current use (its opportunity cost).', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Economic rent', 'any payment to a factor of production above its transfer earnings.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Multiplier', 'the ratio of a change in equilibrium national income to the initial change in injections (spending) that caused it.', 'Labour markets and income distribution'),
  ('Average propensity to save (APS)', 'the proportion of total income that is saved.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Marginal propensity to save (MPS)', 'the proportion of an additional unit of income that is saved.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Average propensity to consume (APC)', 'the proportion of total income that is spent on consumption.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Marginal propensity to consume (MPC)', 'the proportion of an additional unit of income that is spent on consumption.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Average propensity to import (APM)', 'the proportion of total income spent on imports.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Marginal propensity to import (MPM)', 'the proportion of an additional unit of income spent on imports.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
