  ('Induced consumption', 'consumption that varies directly with the level of income.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Savings function', 'the relationship between the level of saving and the level of income.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Autonomous investment', 'investment unrelated to the current level of income/output.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Induced investment', 'investment that varies with the level of income/output.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Accelerator (accelerator theory)', 'the theory that the level of investment depends on the rate of change of national income/output (rather than its level).', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Full employment level of national income', 'the level of national income at which all available resources are fully employed.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
  ('Inflationary gap', 'occurs when planned aggregate expenditure exceeds the full-employment level of output, creating excess demand and pushing up prices.', 'A Level macroeconomics'),
