  ('Secondary sector', 'the part of the economy involved in manufacturing and construction.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Tertiary sector', 'the part of the economy involved in providing services.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('International aid', 'the transfer of resources (money, goods, technical assistance) from one country/organisation to another to support development.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Bilateral aid', 'aid given directly from one country''s government to another.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Multilateral aid', 'aid given by several countries through an international organisation (e.g. the World Bank).', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Multinational company (MNC)', 'a firm that owns/operates production facilities in more than one country.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)', 'investment by a firm or individual in one country into business interests (e.g. production facilities) in another country.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('External debt', 'money owed by a country''s government, corporations or citizens to foreign creditors.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('International Monetary Fund (IMF)', 'an international organisation that promotes global monetary cooperation, financial stability and provides financial assistance to member countries facing balance of payments problems.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('World Bank', 'an international organisation that provides financial and technical assistance to developing countries for development projects.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Globalisation', 'the increasing integration and interdependence of national economies through trade, investment, capital flows, migration and the spread of technology.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Free trade area', 'a group of countries that abolish tariffs/trade barriers between themselves but retain independent trade policies with non-members.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Customs union', 'a free trade area with, additionally, a common external tariff applied to non-member countries.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Monetary union', 'a group of countries that share a common currency and monetary policy.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Economic union (full economic union)', 'the deepest form of integration, combining a customs union, free movement of factors of production, common economic policies and often a common currency.', 'International economics and development'),
  ('Trade creation', 'occurs when trade shifts from a higher-cost domestic producer to a lower-cost producer within a trading bloc, increasing economic welfare.', 'International economics and development'),
